i915: provide intel_pxp_gsccs_is_ready_for_sessions() when PXP is disabled

intel_pxp.c (built unconditionally upstream) calls intel_pxp_gsccs_is_ready_for_sessions(), defined only
in intel_pxp_gsccs.c, which is built with CONFIG_DRM_I915_PXP.  Upstream links because the caller sits
behind intel_pxp_is_enabled(), which is constant false without PXP, and gcc inlines it and removes the
call.  The illumos kernel flags (-fno-inline-small-functions -fno-inline-functions-called-once,
build/Makefile.master) keep the call, so the symbol stays unresolved.  The header now gives the function
a static inline "false" body when PXP is off, as it already does for intel_pxp_gsccs_init() and _fini().

Upstream: candidate (fixes builds that do not inline across the PXP-disabled path)

diff --git a/i915/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/pxp/intel_pxp_gsccs.h b/i915/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/pxp/intel_pxp_gsccs.h
index 9aae779..fc95b27 100644
--- a/i915/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/pxp/intel_pxp_gsccs.h
+++ b/i915/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/pxp/intel_pxp_gsccs.h
@@ -36,6 +36,13 @@ static inline int intel_pxp_gsccs_init(struct intel_pxp *pxp)
 
 #endif
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_DRM_I915_PXP
 bool intel_pxp_gsccs_is_ready_for_sessions(struct intel_pxp *pxp);
+#else
+static inline bool intel_pxp_gsccs_is_ready_for_sessions(struct intel_pxp *pxp)
+{
+	return false;
+}
+#endif
 
 #endif /*__INTEL_PXP_GSCCS_H__ */
